{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbnE27Kn9KeFrhBTCvnn", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Flags here are simple, and the code matches the stored convention.\n\n**How it works**\n- `flags.toml` at the repo root has a `[flags]` table of `name = true/false`. It currently holds one flag, `invoice-pdf-v2 = false`.\n- `src/flags.py` loads that file once at import time. It exposes `is_on(name)`, which returns `False` for any flag not in the file, and `all_flags()`.\n- The convention is to read flags only through `flags.is_on(\"name\")`. Names are kebab-case and must be declared in `flags.toml`.\n\n**For the new checkout flow**\n1. Add the flag to `flags.toml`, defaulting to off:\n   ```toml\n   [flags]\n   invoice-pdf-v2 = false\n   checkout-v2 = false\n   ```\n2. Branch on it where checkout is wired up:\n   ```python\n   from src import flags\n\n   if flags.is_on(\"checkout-v2\"):\n       ...  # new flow\n   else:\n       ...  # existing flow\n   ```\n   Check how other modules import `flags`, since I only found the definition and no call sites yet.\n\n**Caveats**\n- Flags are read from the file at import time, so changing a value needs a restart or redeploy. There are no per-user, percentage or runtime toggles.\n- A typo in a flag name silently returns `False` instead of raising an error, so keep the name identical in both places.\n\nI haven't made any changes. Want me to add the `checkout-v2` entry? If you give me the checkout entry point, I can also add the branch there. I'd name it `checkout-v2` unless you prefer something else."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 887, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24631, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 887}, "output_tokens": 527, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}